PREFIX dcterms: <http://purl.org/dc/terms/>
PREFIX ex: <http://example.com/ns#>
PREFIX rdf: <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#>
PREFIX rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#>
PREFIX sh: <http://www.w3.org/ns/shacl#>
PREFIX skos: <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#>
PREFIX xsd: <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#>

ex:SKOSNullProfileSG
    a sh:ShapesGraph ;
    rdfs:label "SHACL Shapes Graph for SKOS" ;
    dcterms:source
        <https://www.w3.org/2009/08/skos-reference/skos.rdf> ,
        <https://www.w3.org/TR/skos-reference/> ;
    rdfs:comment """Scope and execution
These SHACL Core and SHACL-SPARQL shapes cover the instance-level consequences
of every RDFS/OWL axiom in the SKOS core ontology (S1-S46). SKOS-XL, the separate
optional vocabulary in Appendix B, is outside this graph's scope. The six
conditions expressed only in comments in that ontology (S12, S13, S14, S27, S36,
S46) are also implemented. Each shape cites its SKOS semantic condition.

This is a graph-validation translation, not a general OWL consistency checker.
Domain, range, subclass, subproperty, inverse, symmetry and transitivity shapes
check that the corresponding types and triples are present in the validation
graph. Missing entailed triples are completeness failures here, not OWL logical
contradictions. For ordinary SKOS integrity checking, first materialize the SKOS
core RDFS/OWL entailments using the official ontology, including inverse,
symmetric and transitive triples. Otherwise these shapes deliberately report
missing entailments. No ontology import, network access, SHACL rules or particular
processor inference mode is required by this file itself. SHACL-SPARQL support
is required. Custom subproperties/subclasses need their own schema entailments.

SHACL counts distinct RDF terms. For S35, OWL functionality instead permits
multiple object names denoting one individual. Canonicalize known owl:sameAs
aliases before validation if OWL identity semantics are needed. Unknown identity
cannot be decided by these shapes. Similarly, missing assertions in an open-world
dataset do not by themselves establish OWL inconsistency.

S1, S2 and S28 declare classes; S3, S18, S30 and S38 declare object properties;
S10 and S16 declare annotation properties; S15 declares a datatype property.
The class declarations alone impose no extra instance constraint. Object-property
and datatype-property value kinds are checked. Annotation-property declarations
alone impose no domain, range, cardinality or value-kind restriction. Consequently
labels and notes are not restricted to concepts, notes may be literals or
resources, and skos:inScheme has no imposed domain. Vocabulary declarations do
not have to be copied into each data graph. S29 is checked as subclass membership;
S32 uses sh:or for the OWL union range. There are no other OWL restrictions,
keys, property chains or cardinality axioms in the core ontology.

RDF 1.1 plain labels are represented by xsd:string or rdf:langString (S12).
S14 includes the ontology comment's at-most-one untagged preferred label as well
as at-most-one per language, with language tags compared case-insensitively.
S27 and S46 inspect relevant inverse, subproperty and transitive paths directly,
so indirect clashes are found even before closure. S36 checks every list item
against skos:member; list well-formedness is a separate optional check below.

Additional constraints that could be implemented:

The following are proposals only, not active shapes and not additional normative
SKOS integrity conditions. Adding them would define a stricter application profile.

1. Notation uniqueness within a concept scheme (6.5.3, #L2646): detect distinct
concepts in the same scheme sharing a notation, with a documented policy for
literal identity, datatype and equivalent concept identities.
2. Notation datatype conventions (6.5.1, #L2613): require a datatype identifying
the notation system and reject language-tagged notations. S15 itself only
requires a literal; SKOS does not prescribe a particular notation datatype.
3. Top-concept placement (4.6.3): flag a top concept having a broader concept
within the same scheme. This follows the intended entry-point meaning but is
explicitly not a formal SKOS integrity condition.
4. Direct hierarchy links (8.6.6): flag skos:broader/skos:narrower edges that
duplicate a longer hierarchy path. The immediate-link convention is not an OWL
transitivity axiom for these properties, and intentional alternate paths are valid.
5. Hierarchy self-links and cycles (8.6.7-8.6.8): warn about self-parent links
or cycles. SKOS permits these; do not silently impose irreflexivity or acyclicity.
6. Mapping scope (10.6.1): check mapping endpoints against known concept schemes
and warn when a mapping is internal to a scheme. SKOS does not formally limit
mapping use to different schemes; concepts can belong to multiple schemes.
7. RDF list structure (9.6.2): require finite, rdf:nil-terminated, unbranched
member lists with exactly one rdf:first and rdf:rest on each non-nil cell and
none on rdf:nil. SKOS does not itself impose these syntactic list restrictions.
8. Abstract relation use (skos:semanticRelation scope note): discourage direct
assertions of the generic property in source data. Run this check before inference,
because legitimate specific relations entail semanticRelation triples.
9. Label usage (5.6.4-5.6.5): an application may require preferred labels when
alternate/hidden labels occur, or require selected languages. SKOS permits
alternate labels without preferred labels and permits untagged plain labels.
10. Documentation completeness (7.1, 7.5): an application may require definitions
or scope notes. SKOS does not require these, limit their count, or restrict all
documentation values to literals.

Do not add a mandatory scheme for every concept, a domain of skos:Concept for
skos:inScheme, a same-scheme requirement for semantic relations, transitivity for
skos:broader or skos:closeMatch, equivalence with owl:sameAs for skos:exactMatch,
or an exact-one memberList requirement: none follows from the SKOS core axioms.
""" ;
    rdfs:member
        ex:AltLabelLabelSubpropertyShape ,
        ex:BroadMatchBroaderSubpropertyShape ,
        ex:BroadMatchInverseShape ,
        ex:BroadMatchMappingRelationSubpropertyShape ,
        ex:BroaderBroaderTransitiveSubpropertyShape ,
        ex:BroaderInverseShape ,
        ex:BroaderTransitiveInverseShape ,
        ex:BroaderTransitiveSemanticRelationSubpropertyShape ,
        ex:BroaderTransitiveTransitivityShape ,
        ex:ChangeNoteNoteSubpropertyShape ,
        ex:CloseMatchMappingRelationSubpropertyShape ,
        ex:CloseMatchSymmetryShape ,
        ex:CollectionConceptDisjointShape ,
        ex:CollectionConceptSchemeDisjointShape ,
        ex:ConceptConceptSchemeDisjointShape ,
        ex:DefinitionNoteSubpropertyShape ,
        ex:DisjointLabelsShape ,
        ex:EditorialNoteNoteSubpropertyShape ,
        ex:ExactMatchCloseMatchSubpropertyShape ,
        ex:ExactMatchDisjointShape ,
        ex:ExactMatchSymmetryShape ,
        ex:ExactMatchTransitivityShape ,
        ex:ExampleNoteSubpropertyShape ,
        ex:HasTopConceptDomainShape ,
        ex:HasTopConceptInverseShape ,
        ex:HasTopConceptRangeShape ,
        ex:HiddenLabelLabelSubpropertyShape ,
        ex:HistoryNoteNoteSubpropertyShape ,
        ex:InSchemeRangeShape ,
        ex:MappingRelationSemanticRelationSubpropertyShape ,
        ex:MemberDomainShape ,
        ex:MemberListDomainShape ,
        ex:MemberListFunctionalShape ,
        ex:MemberListMembershipShape ,
        ex:MemberListRangeShape ,
        ex:MemberRangeShape ,
        ex:NarrowMatchInverseShape ,
        ex:NarrowMatchMappingRelationSubpropertyShape ,
        ex:NarrowMatchNarrowerSubpropertyShape ,
        ex:NarrowerInverseShape ,
        ex:NarrowerNarrowerTransitiveSubpropertyShape ,
        ex:NarrowerTransitiveInverseShape ,
        ex:NarrowerTransitiveSemanticRelationSubpropertyShape ,
        ex:NarrowerTransitiveTransitivityShape ,
        ex:NotationRangeShape ,
        ex:ObjectPropertyRangeShape ,
        ex:OrderedCollectionConceptDisjointShape ,
        ex:OrderedCollectionConceptSchemeDisjointShape ,
        ex:OrderedCollectionSubclassShape ,
        ex:PlainLabelRangeShape ,
        ex:PrefLabelLabelSubpropertyShape ,
        ex:PreferredLabelLanguageShape ,
        ex:RelatedHierarchyDisjointShape ,
        ex:RelatedMatchMappingRelationSubpropertyShape ,
        ex:RelatedMatchRelatedSubpropertyShape ,
        ex:RelatedMatchSymmetryShape ,
        ex:RelatedSemanticRelationSubpropertyShape ,
        ex:RelatedSymmetryShape ,
        ex:ScopeNoteNoteSubpropertyShape ,
        ex:SemanticRelationDomainShape ,
        ex:SemanticRelationRangeShape ,
        ex:TopConceptOfDomainShape ,
        ex:TopConceptOfInSchemeSubpropertyShape ,
        ex:TopConceptOfInverseShape ,
        ex:TopConceptOfRangeShape ;
.

ex:AltLabelLabelSubpropertyShape
    a sh:NodeShape ;
    rdfs:label "AltLabelLabelSubproperty" ;
    dcterms:source <https://www.w3.org/TR/skos-reference/#S11> ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy ex:SKOSNullProfile ;
    sh:message "A subproperty assertion requires its corresponding superproperty assertion." ;
    sh:sparql
        [
            sh:message "A skos:altLabel assertion requires the same value for rdfs:label." ;
            sh:select """PREFIX skos: <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#>
SELECT DISTINCT $this ?path ?value WHERE {
    $this skos:altLabel ?value .
    BIND (rdfs:label AS ?path)
    FILTER NOT EXISTS { $this rdfs:label ?value }
}""" ;
        ] ;
    sh:targetSubjectsOf skos:altLabel ;
.

ex:BroadMatchBroaderSubpropertyShape
    a sh:NodeShape ;
    rdfs:label "BroadMatchBroaderSubproperty" ;
    dcterms:source <https://www.w3.org/TR/skos-reference/#S41> ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy ex:SKOSNullProfile ;
    sh:message "A subproperty assertion requires its corresponding superproperty assertion." ;
    sh:sparql
        [
            sh:message "A skos:broadMatch assertion requires the same value for skos:broader." ;
            sh:select """PREFIX skos: <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#>
SELECT DISTINCT $this ?path ?value WHERE {
    $this skos:broadMatch ?value .
    BIND (skos:broader AS ?path)
    FILTER NOT EXISTS { $this skos:broader ?value }
}""" ;
        ] ;
    sh:targetSubjectsOf skos:broadMatch ;
.

ex:BroadMatchInverseShape
    a sh:NodeShape ;
    rdfs:label "BroadMatchInverse" ;
    dcterms:source <https://www.w3.org/TR/skos-reference/#S43> ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy ex:SKOSNullProfile ;
    sh:message "An inverse-property assertion must have its corresponding reverse assertion." ;
    sh:sparql
        [
            sh:message "Each skos:broadMatch assertion requires its inverse skos:narrowMatch assertion." ;
            sh:select """PREFIX skos: <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#>
SELECT DISTINCT $this ?path ?value WHERE {
    $this skos:broadMatch ?value .
    BIND (skos:broadMatch AS ?path)
    FILTER NOT EXISTS { ?value skos:narrowMatch $this }
}""" ;
        ] ;
    sh:targetSubjectsOf skos:broadMatch ;
.

ex:BroadMatchMappingRelationSubpropertyShape
    a sh:NodeShape ;
    rdfs:label "BroadMatchMappingRelationSubproperty" ;
    dcterms:source <https://www.w3.org/TR/skos-reference/#S40> ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy ex:SKOSNullProfile ;
    sh:message "A subproperty assertion requires its corresponding superproperty assertion." ;
    sh:sparql
        [
            sh:message "A skos:broadMatch assertion requires the same value for skos:mappingRelation." ;
            sh:select """PREFIX skos: <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#>
SELECT DISTINCT $this ?path ?value WHERE {
    $this skos:broadMatch ?value .
    BIND (skos:mappingRelation AS ?path)
    FILTER NOT EXISTS { $this skos:mappingRelation ?value }
}""" ;
        ] ;
    sh:targetSubjectsOf skos:broadMatch ;
.

ex:BroaderBroaderTransitiveSubpropertyShape
    a sh:NodeShape ;
    rdfs:label "BroaderBroaderTransitiveSubproperty" ;
    dcterms:source <https://www.w3.org/TR/skos-reference/#S22> ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy ex:SKOSNullProfile ;
    sh:message "A subproperty assertion requires its corresponding superproperty assertion." ;
    sh:sparql
        [
            sh:message "A skos:broader assertion requires the same value for skos:broaderTransitive." ;
            sh:select """PREFIX skos: <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#>
SELECT DISTINCT $this ?path ?value WHERE {
    $this skos:broader ?value .
    BIND (skos:broaderTransitive AS ?path)
    FILTER NOT EXISTS { $this skos:broaderTransitive ?value }
}""" ;
        ] ;
    sh:targetSubjectsOf skos:broader ;
.

ex:BroaderInverseShape
    a sh:NodeShape ;
    rdfs:label "BroaderInverse" ;
    dcterms:source <https://www.w3.org/TR/skos-reference/#S25> ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy ex:SKOSNullProfile ;
    sh:message "An inverse-property assertion must have its corresponding reverse assertion." ;
    sh:sparql
        [
            sh:message "Each skos:broader assertion requires its inverse skos:narrower assertion." ;
            sh:select """PREFIX skos: <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#>
SELECT DISTINCT $this ?path ?value WHERE {
    $this skos:broader ?value .
    BIND (skos:broader AS ?path)
    FILTER NOT EXISTS { ?value skos:narrower $this }
}""" ;
        ] ;
    sh:targetSubjectsOf skos:broader ;
.

ex:BroaderTransitiveInverseShape
    a sh:NodeShape ;
    rdfs:label "BroaderTransitiveInverse" ;
    dcterms:source <https://www.w3.org/TR/skos-reference/#S26> ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy ex:SKOSNullProfile ;
    sh:message "An inverse-property assertion must have its corresponding reverse assertion." ;
    sh:sparql
        [
            sh:message "Each skos:broaderTransitive assertion requires its inverse skos:narrowerTransitive assertion." ;
            sh:select """PREFIX skos: <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#>
SELECT DISTINCT $this ?path ?value WHERE {
    $this skos:broaderTransitive ?value .
    BIND (skos:broaderTransitive AS ?path)
    FILTER NOT EXISTS { ?value skos:narrowerTransitive $this }
}""" ;
        ] ;
    sh:targetSubjectsOf skos:broaderTransitive ;
.

ex:BroaderTransitiveSemanticRelationSubpropertyShape
    a sh:NodeShape ;
    rdfs:label "BroaderTransitiveSemanticRelationSubproperty" ;
    dcterms:source <https://www.w3.org/TR/skos-reference/#S21> ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy ex:SKOSNullProfile ;
    sh:message "A subproperty assertion requires its corresponding superproperty assertion." ;
    sh:sparql
        [
            sh:message "A skos:broaderTransitive assertion requires the same value for skos:semanticRelation." ;
            sh:select """PREFIX skos: <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#>
SELECT DISTINCT $this ?path ?value WHERE {
    $this skos:broaderTransitive ?value .
    BIND (skos:semanticRelation AS ?path)
    FILTER NOT EXISTS { $this skos:semanticRelation ?value }
}""" ;
        ] ;
    sh:targetSubjectsOf skos:broaderTransitive ;
.

ex:BroaderTransitiveTransitivityShape
    a sh:NodeShape ;
    rdfs:label "BroaderTransitiveTransitivity" ;
    dcterms:source <https://www.w3.org/TR/skos-reference/#S24> ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy ex:SKOSNullProfile ;
    sh:message "skos:broaderTransitive must include the triples implied by transitivity." ;
    sh:sparql
        [
            sh:message "A two-step skos:broaderTransitive path requires its direct transitive assertion." ;
            sh:select """PREFIX skos: <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#>
SELECT DISTINCT $this ?path ?value WHERE {
    $this skos:broaderTransitive/skos:broaderTransitive ?value .
    BIND (skos:broaderTransitive AS ?path)
    FILTER NOT EXISTS { $this skos:broaderTransitive ?value }
}""" ;
        ] ;
    sh:targetSubjectsOf skos:broaderTransitive ;
.

ex:ChangeNoteNoteSubpropertyShape
    a sh:NodeShape ;
    rdfs:label "ChangeNoteNoteSubproperty" ;
    dcterms:source <https://www.w3.org/TR/skos-reference/#S17> ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy ex:SKOSNullProfile ;
    sh:message "A subproperty assertion requires its corresponding superproperty assertion." ;
    sh:sparql
        [
            sh:message "A skos:changeNote assertion requires the same value for skos:note." ;
            sh:select """PREFIX skos: <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#>
SELECT DISTINCT $this ?path ?value WHERE {
    $this skos:changeNote ?value .
    BIND (skos:note AS ?path)
    FILTER NOT EXISTS { $this skos:note ?value }
}""" ;
        ] ;
    sh:targetSubjectsOf skos:changeNote ;
.

ex:CloseMatchMappingRelationSubpropertyShape
    a sh:NodeShape ;
    rdfs:label "CloseMatchMappingRelationSubproperty" ;
    dcterms:source <https://www.w3.org/TR/skos-reference/#S40> ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy ex:SKOSNullProfile ;
    sh:message "A subproperty assertion requires its corresponding superproperty assertion." ;
    sh:sparql
        [
            sh:message "A skos:closeMatch assertion requires the same value for skos:mappingRelation." ;
            sh:select """PREFIX skos: <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#>
SELECT DISTINCT $this ?path ?value WHERE {
    $this skos:closeMatch ?value .
    BIND (skos:mappingRelation AS ?path)
    FILTER NOT EXISTS { $this skos:mappingRelation ?value }
}""" ;
        ] ;
    sh:targetSubjectsOf skos:closeMatch ;
.

ex:CloseMatchSymmetryShape
    a sh:NodeShape ;
    rdfs:label "CloseMatchSymmetry" ;
    dcterms:source <https://www.w3.org/TR/skos-reference/#S44> ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy ex:SKOSNullProfile ;
    sh:message "skos:closeMatch requires a reverse assertion of the same property." ;
    sh:sparql
        [
            sh:message "skos:closeMatch is symmetric." ;
            sh:select """PREFIX skos: <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#>
SELECT DISTINCT $this ?path ?value WHERE {
    $this skos:closeMatch ?value .
    BIND (skos:closeMatch AS ?path)
    FILTER NOT EXISTS { ?value skos:closeMatch $this }
}""" ;
        ] ;
    sh:targetSubjectsOf skos:closeMatch ;
.

ex:CollectionConceptDisjointShape
    a sh:NodeShape ;
    rdfs:label "CollectionConceptDisjoint" ;
    dcterms:source <https://www.w3.org/TR/skos-reference/#S37> ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy ex:SKOSNullProfile ;
    sh:message "skos:Collection and skos:Concept have disjoint instances." ;
    sh:not
        [
            sh:class skos:Concept ;
        ] ;
    sh:targetClass skos:Collection ;
.

ex:CollectionConceptSchemeDisjointShape
    a sh:NodeShape ;
    rdfs:label "CollectionConceptSchemeDisjoint" ;
    dcterms:source <https://www.w3.org/TR/skos-reference/#S37> ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy ex:SKOSNullProfile ;
    sh:message "skos:Collection and skos:ConceptScheme have disjoint instances." ;
    sh:not
        [
            sh:class skos:ConceptScheme ;
        ] ;
    sh:targetClass skos:Collection ;
.

ex:CollectionValueShape
    sh:class skos:Collection ;
.

ex:ConceptConceptSchemeDisjointShape
    a sh:NodeShape ;
    rdfs:label "ConceptConceptSchemeDisjoint" ;
    dcterms:source <https://www.w3.org/TR/skos-reference/#S9> ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy ex:SKOSNullProfile ;
    sh:message "skos:Concept and skos:ConceptScheme have disjoint instances." ;
    sh:not
        [
            sh:class skos:ConceptScheme ;
        ] ;
    sh:targetClass skos:Concept ;
.

ex:ConceptValueShape
    sh:class skos:Concept ;
.

ex:DefinitionNoteSubpropertyShape
    a sh:NodeShape ;
    rdfs:label "DefinitionNoteSubproperty" ;
    dcterms:source <https://www.w3.org/TR/skos-reference/#S17> ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy ex:SKOSNullProfile ;
    sh:message "A subproperty assertion requires its corresponding superproperty assertion." ;
    sh:sparql
        [
            sh:message "A skos:definition assertion requires the same value for skos:note." ;
            sh:select """PREFIX skos: <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#>
SELECT DISTINCT $this ?path ?value WHERE {
    $this skos:definition ?value .
    BIND (skos:note AS ?path)
    FILTER NOT EXISTS { $this skos:note ?value }
}""" ;
        ] ;
    sh:targetSubjectsOf skos:definition ;
.

ex:DisjointLabelsAltLabelhiddenLabelPropertyShape
    sh:disjoint skos:hiddenLabel ;
    sh:path skos:altLabel ;
.

ex:DisjointLabelsPrefLabelaltLabelPropertyShape
    sh:disjoint skos:altLabel ;
    sh:path skos:prefLabel ;
.

ex:DisjointLabelsPrefLabelhiddenLabelPropertyShape
    sh:disjoint skos:hiddenLabel ;
    sh:path skos:prefLabel ;
.

ex:DisjointLabelsShape
    a sh:NodeShape ;
    rdfs:label "DisjointLabels" ;
    dcterms:source <https://www.w3.org/TR/skos-reference/#S13> ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy ex:SKOSNullProfile ;
    sh:message "A label value cannot be used in two different SKOS lexical labeling properties on one resource." ;
    sh:property
        ex:DisjointLabelsAltLabelhiddenLabelPropertyShape ,
        ex:DisjointLabelsPrefLabelaltLabelPropertyShape ,
        ex:DisjointLabelsPrefLabelhiddenLabelPropertyShape ;
    sh:targetSubjectsOf
        skos:altLabel ,
        skos:hiddenLabel ,
        skos:prefLabel ;
.

ex:EditorialNoteNoteSubpropertyShape
    a sh:NodeShape ;
    rdfs:label "EditorialNoteNoteSubproperty" ;
    dcterms:source <https://www.w3.org/TR/skos-reference/#S17> ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy ex:SKOSNullProfile ;
    sh:message "A subproperty assertion requires its corresponding superproperty assertion." ;
    sh:sparql
        [
            sh:message "A skos:editorialNote assertion requires the same value for skos:note." ;
            sh:select """PREFIX skos: <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#>
SELECT DISTINCT $this ?path ?value WHERE {
    $this skos:editorialNote ?value .
    BIND (skos:note AS ?path)
    FILTER NOT EXISTS { $this skos:note ?value }
}""" ;
        ] ;
    sh:targetSubjectsOf skos:editorialNote ;
.

ex:ExactMatchCloseMatchSubpropertyShape
    a sh:NodeShape ;
    rdfs:label "ExactMatchCloseMatchSubproperty" ;
    dcterms:source <https://www.w3.org/TR/skos-reference/#S42> ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy ex:SKOSNullProfile ;
    sh:message "A subproperty assertion requires its corresponding superproperty assertion." ;
    sh:sparql
        [
            sh:message "A skos:exactMatch assertion requires the same value for skos:closeMatch." ;
            sh:select """PREFIX skos: <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#>
SELECT DISTINCT $this ?path ?value WHERE {
    $this skos:exactMatch ?value .
    BIND (skos:closeMatch AS ?path)
    FILTER NOT EXISTS { $this skos:closeMatch ?value }
}""" ;
        ] ;
    sh:targetSubjectsOf skos:exactMatch ;
.

ex:ExactMatchDisjointShape
    a sh:NodeShape ;
    rdfs:label "ExactMatchDisjoint" ;
    dcterms:source <https://www.w3.org/TR/skos-reference/#S46> ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy ex:SKOSNullProfile ;
    sh:message "skos:exactMatch cannot overlap skos:broadMatch or skos:relatedMatch." ;
    sh:sparql
        [
            sh:message "An exactMatch pair also has a broadMatch/narrowMatch or relatedMatch relation (S46)." ;
            sh:select """PREFIX skos: <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#>
SELECT DISTINCT $this ?path ?value WHERE {
    $this (skos:exactMatch|^skos:exactMatch)+ ?value .
    $this (skos:broadMatch|^skos:narrowMatch|skos:relatedMatch|^skos:relatedMatch) ?value .
    BIND (skos:exactMatch AS ?path)
}""" ;
        ] ;
    sh:targetObjectsOf skos:exactMatch ;
    sh:targetSubjectsOf skos:exactMatch ;
.

ex:ExactMatchSymmetryShape
    a sh:NodeShape ;
    rdfs:label "ExactMatchSymmetry" ;
    dcterms:source <https://www.w3.org/TR/skos-reference/#S44> ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy ex:SKOSNullProfile ;
    sh:message "skos:exactMatch requires a reverse assertion of the same property." ;
    sh:sparql
        [
            sh:message "skos:exactMatch is symmetric." ;
            sh:select """PREFIX skos: <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#>
SELECT DISTINCT $this ?path ?value WHERE {
    $this skos:exactMatch ?value .
    BIND (skos:exactMatch AS ?path)
    FILTER NOT EXISTS { ?value skos:exactMatch $this }
}""" ;
        ] ;
    sh:targetSubjectsOf skos:exactMatch ;
.

ex:ExactMatchTransitivityShape
    a sh:NodeShape ;
    rdfs:label "ExactMatchTransitivity" ;
    dcterms:source <https://www.w3.org/TR/skos-reference/#S45> ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy ex:SKOSNullProfile ;
    sh:message "skos:exactMatch must include the triples implied by transitivity." ;
    sh:sparql
        [
            sh:message "A two-step skos:exactMatch path requires its direct transitive assertion." ;
            sh:select """PREFIX skos: <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#>
SELECT DISTINCT $this ?path ?value WHERE {
    $this skos:exactMatch/skos:exactMatch ?value .
    BIND (skos:exactMatch AS ?path)
    FILTER NOT EXISTS { $this skos:exactMatch ?value }
}""" ;
        ] ;
    sh:targetSubjectsOf skos:exactMatch ;
.

ex:ExampleNoteSubpropertyShape
    a sh:NodeShape ;
    rdfs:label "ExampleNoteSubproperty" ;
    dcterms:source <https://www.w3.org/TR/skos-reference/#S17> ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy ex:SKOSNullProfile ;
    sh:message "A subproperty assertion requires its corresponding superproperty assertion." ;
    sh:sparql
        [
            sh:message "A skos:example assertion requires the same value for skos:note." ;
            sh:select """PREFIX skos: <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#>
SELECT DISTINCT $this ?path ?value WHERE {
    $this skos:example ?value .
    BIND (skos:note AS ?path)
    FILTER NOT EXISTS { $this skos:note ?value }
}""" ;
        ] ;
    sh:targetSubjectsOf skos:example ;
.

ex:HasTopConceptDomainShape
    a sh:NodeShape ;
    rdfs:label "HasTopConceptDomain" ;
    dcterms:source <https://www.w3.org/TR/skos-reference/#S5> ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy ex:SKOSNullProfile ;
    sh:class skos:ConceptScheme ;
    sh:message "The domain of skos:hasTopConcept must satisfy its SKOS class constraint." ;
    sh:targetSubjectsOf skos:hasTopConcept ;
.

ex:HasTopConceptInverseShape
    a sh:NodeShape ;
    rdfs:label "HasTopConceptInverse" ;
    dcterms:source <https://www.w3.org/TR/skos-reference/#S8> ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy ex:SKOSNullProfile ;
    sh:message "An inverse-property assertion must have its corresponding reverse assertion." ;
    sh:sparql
        [
            sh:message "Each skos:hasTopConcept assertion requires its inverse skos:topConceptOf assertion." ;
            sh:select """PREFIX skos: <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#>
SELECT DISTINCT $this ?path ?value WHERE {
    $this skos:hasTopConcept ?value .
    BIND (skos:hasTopConcept AS ?path)
    FILTER NOT EXISTS { ?value skos:topConceptOf $this }
}""" ;
        ] ;
    sh:targetSubjectsOf skos:hasTopConcept ;
.

ex:HasTopConceptRangeShape
    a sh:NodeShape ;
    rdfs:label "HasTopConceptRange" ;
    dcterms:source <https://www.w3.org/TR/skos-reference/#S6> ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy ex:SKOSNullProfile ;
    sh:class skos:Concept ;
    sh:message "The range of skos:hasTopConcept must satisfy its SKOS class constraint." ;
    sh:targetObjectsOf skos:hasTopConcept ;
.

ex:HiddenLabelLabelSubpropertyShape
    a sh:NodeShape ;
